# fastly_service_logging_newrelicotlp (Resource)

Fastly service New Relic OTLP logging endpoint resource. Writes directly to the specified writable service version.

This resource is part of the explicit/default first-class resource family. It
manages a New Relic OTLP real-time logging endpoint on the configured service
version. It does not clone, activate, or stage service versions.

To have the provider manage the version lifecycle for you instead, use the
nested `logging_newrelicotlp` block on `fastly_service_cdn_auto` or
`fastly_service_compute_auto` — see "Automatic-lifecycle usage" below.

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_logging_newrelicotlp" "example" {
  service_id = fastly_service_cdn.example.id
  version    = 1
  name       = "newrelicotlp-us"

  authentication = {
    token = var.newrelic_api_key
  }
  region = "US"
}
```

A fully configured endpoint, streaming to a custom Trace Observer URL for
Infinite Tracing. `format`, `format_version`, `placement`, and
`response_condition` only affect generated VCL, so they are valid when
`service_id` refers to a CDN (VCL) service and rejected for a Compute service:

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_logging_newrelicotlp" "eu" {
  service_id = fastly_service_cdn.example.id
  version    = 1
  name       = "newrelicotlp-eu"

  authentication = {
    token = var.newrelic_api_key
  }
  region            = "EU"
  url               = "https://otlp.eu01.nr-data.net:4318/v1/logs"
  processing_region = "eu"

  format             = "%h %l %u %t \"%r\" %>s %b"
  format_version     = 2
  placement          = "none"
  response_condition = fastly_service_condition.errors_only.name
}
```

Attaching to a Compute service — the VCL-only attributes must be omitted:

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_logging_newrelicotlp" "compute" {
  service_id = fastly_service_compute.example.id
  version    = 1
  name       = "newrelicotlp-compute"

  authentication = {
    token = var.newrelic_api_key
  }
  region = "US"
}
```

## Automatic-lifecycle usage

Inside the `_auto` service resources, New Relic OTLP logging is a nested block
and the provider clones, validates, and activates a new service version
whenever the block changes. The nested block takes the same arguments as this
resource, minus `service_id` and `version`, which the parent service owns.

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_cdn_auto" "example" {
  name = "my-service"

  logging_newrelicotlp {
    name = "newrelicotlp-us"
    authentication = {
      token = var.newrelic_api_key
    }
    region = "US"
  }
}
```

`fastly_service_compute_auto` supports the same block, without the VCL-only
arguments (`format`, `format_version`, `placement`, `response_condition`):

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_compute_auto" "example" {
  name = "my-compute-service"

  package {
    filename         = "package.tar.gz"
    source_code_hash = filesha512("package.tar.gz")
  }

  logging_newrelicotlp {
    name = "newrelicotlp-compute"
    authentication = {
      token = var.newrelic_api_key
    }
    region = "US"
  }
}
```

